===persian===

ای... آن پر طراوتِ بارانی
مهتابِ بی‌دریغِ بیابانی
چون از سفر به چشمِ تو برگردم
با شعله‌های آتشِ پنهانی
هر برگ در نگاهِ تَرَم باغی‌ست
هر غنچه شهرِ شادِ چراغانی.

بهار ۱۳۶۸

===machine===

Oh... that rainy freshness
The unsparing moonlight of the desert
When I return from my journey to your eyes
With the flames of a hidden fire
Every leaf in my wet gaze is a garden
Every bud a joyous, illuminated city.

Spring 1368

===lantern===

O you — that rain-freshened, dewy grace,
the desert's unstinting moonlit face:
when I come home from the journey to your eyes
bearing the flames of a hidden fire,
every leaf in my brimming gaze is a garden,
every bud a glad city ablaze with light.

— Spring 1368

===translation===

===footnotes===

The only formally classical piece in this group: a rhymed, metrical fragment in the manner of a ghazal, the line-ends chiming بارانی / بیابانی / پنهانی / چراغانی (-âni). The lantern reaches for a little of that music (grace / face) without forcing the full mono-rhyme. چراغانی is the festival lighting-up of a city — lamps strung for celebration — so the closing bud opens like a town lit for a feast. نگاهِ تَر, "the wet/moist gaze," is a gaze brimming to tears with feeling, not with grief.
